EXTENSION "ArM5_The_Lion_and_the_Lily_ChampagneAndBurgundy_EloiFollowerOfJerbiton" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Lion and the Lily - Eloi, Follower of Jerbiton"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_The_Lion_and_the_Lily_Core_Ext"

    # Eloi, Follower of Jerbiton (Chapter Nine: Champagne and Burgundy, p109): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t8b7511971a340231cf638b ^"Eloi, Follower of Jerbiton" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#tdc4bd16737c7f4eef04a98 ^"Cunfin"]
            ^"Age" STRING "62 (Apparent age: 52)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Pious +3, Diplomatic +3, Forgiving +1"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 109
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Eloi is the lynchpin that holds the covenant of Cunfin together. The monks know him as Brother Eligius, the prior, a man respected for his wise council and beloved for his devotion to God. The magi know him as a man deeply concerned about the Order’s relationship to the Church. Eloi sees himself as a follower of St. Nerius, a man attempting to bridge the gap between the Magical and the Divine. It is his charisma and devotion that binds together Cunfin’s otherwise fractious elements into a workable whole.\n\nA younger son of a minor noble family, Eloi was bound for the church from an early age. His parents intended for him to be a priest, and the boy himself was quite excited by the prospect, but he was found by Jerome of Jerbiton and became a magus instead. While he proved to be a useful tool for Jerome at Confluensis, he was never quite able to reconcile his desire to serve God with his Gift. In 1191, however, he met Angelus, who taught him about St. Nerius. Seeing a way to reconcile his two natures, Eloi moved to Cunfin to join the monastery and founded the covenant. His parens saw this as an opportunity to establish closer ties with the Church, and Eloi agreed. His unique skills and obvious piety led the monks of Cunfin to elect him prior not long after, and he has maintained control of the monastery ever since.\n\nAlthough he is not a member, he has close contacts with the Priory of St. Nerius (see *Realms of Power: The Divine*, page 94). Like them, he seeks to have St. Nerius recognized by the Latin Church, but this is secondary to his goal of maintaining peaceful relations between the Order and the Church. With his influence in the powerful Cistercian order, he seeks to smooth over potential conflicts between magi and the clergy. His current concern is the newly created Dominican Order and their vigorous pursuit of heretics. He hopes to keep them away from the Order of Hermes."
    }

}
